  "sortOrder": 22007,
  "verseCount": 13,
  "aliases": [
    "Song",
    "Song of Songs",
    "SOS",
    "Canticles"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "How beautiful are thy feet with shoes, O prince’s daughter! the joints of thy thighs are like jewels, the work of the hands of a cunning workman.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Thy navel is like a round goblet, which wanteth not liquor: thy belly is like an heap of wheat set about with lilies.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Thy two breasts are like two young roes that are twins.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Thy neck is as a tower of ivory; thine eyes like the fishpools in Heshbon, by the gate of Bathrabbim: thy nose is as the tower of Lebanon which looketh toward Damascus.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Thine head upon thee is like Carmel, and the hair of thine head like purple; the king is held in the galleries.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "How fair and how pleasant art thou, O love, for delights!",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "This thy stature is like to a palm tree, and thy breasts to clusters of grapes.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "I said, I will go up to the palm tree, I will take hold of the boughs thereof: now also thy breasts shall be as clusters of the vine, and the smell of thy nose like apples;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "And the roof of thy mouth like the best wine for my beloved, that goeth down sweetly, causing the lips of those that are asleep to speak.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "I am my beloved’s, and his desire is toward me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Come, my beloved, let us go forth into the field; let us lodge in the villages.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Let us get up early to the vineyards; let us see if the vine flourish, whether the tender grape appear, and the pomegranates bud forth: there will I give thee my loves.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "The mandrakes give a smell, and at our gates are all manner of pleasant fruits, new and old, which I have laid up for thee, O my beloved.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:7:13"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
